  "noMusicReason": "Standing rule (2026-08-24 user directive): reels ship voice + SFX only, no music bed by default. Set plan[\"music\"] = true (or a full music object) to opt this reel back into a bed.",
  "script": "Your next Android phone is about to cost more, and it started today. Here's why.\nQualcomm raised Snapdragon prices, and says it's double digits.\n\nThat's the chip in most premium Android phones, and CEO Cristiano Amon says it's across the board: watches, Arm laptops.\nYou won't feel it in a shop yet. It lands on whoever builds your phone.\n\nAnd that phone's price has almost nothing to do with the chip.\n\nAmon put it plainly: cost went up, prices are going to go up.\nQualcomm's release blames wafers, assembly, packaging. And memory.\n\nThat last word is doing the work.\nAI data centers buy memory faster than anyone makes it.\nTrendForce had conventional DRAM contract prices climbing 58 to 63 percent in a quarter.\nAnd JP Morgan has DRAM up over 400 percent by year end, on AI demand.\n\nSo your phone's price moves with memory more than Snapdragon.\nWhich makes double digits the small number.\n\nOn September 22, Qualcomm unveils its next flagship chip.\nThat's the first one priced this way. It lands in next year's phones.\n\nNo phone maker has named a figure.\nQualcomm expects that in its margins within a couple of quarters. Yours lands much later.\n\nBuying now, or waiting it out?",
